  "baseline": {
    "limits": "These composition controls do not retroactively invalidate f1b's separately qualified6cd scope. Rebound control first refuses the missing metadata limits; later successful explicit comparison is a positive feature control.",
    "production": "unchanged f1b storage commands composed with the exact new0a5 inventory API",
    "test_only_head": "d6e72e859f1c32c215732482e43e763f120bbecd",
    "tree": "3cada7c27a36f4a547270828929df5c8474c4c09"
  },
  "behavior": [
    "Public daemon inventory/verify commands pass explicit bounded owner-attribute count and bytes to inventory-v3, retaining opaque original owner xattrs.",
    "Separate storage-owner-inventory/storage-owner-verify commands accept only explicit owner-local policy; daemon and owner-local scopes reject each other's declarations, and absent/canceled context remains refused.",
    "Verification requires explicit --compare-reviewed-rebound to compare a separately declared replacement root. Exact file and opaque attribute equality never rebinds embedded inodes or authorizes restart.",
    "Busy roots, cancellation, malformed limits, missing retained metadata and short stdout writes refuse a complete successful report; all reports retain restart_authorized=false."
  ],
